@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Deterministic grammar analysis and category-token parsing
hide footbox
autonumber
actor Learner
participant "Compiler lab\n<<React functions>>" as Web
participant "coursework_api / coursework\n<<functions>>" as API
participant "parser.service / analysis / grammar\n<<modules>>" as Grammar
participant "lexer / dataset\n<<modules>>" as Lexer
participant "predictive\n<<module>>" as Parser

Learner -> Web : Analyze corpus or Parse practice input
activate Web
Web -> API : POST /api/coursework/analyze or /parse\ncurrent editor grammar
activate API
API -> Grammar : analyze_grammar(grammar)
activate Grammar
Grammar -> Grammar : read_grammar(); transform_grammar()
activate Grammar
note over Grammar : Validate symbols/limits; ordered substitution,\ndirect recursion elimination, repeated left factoring.\nKeep bounded before/after transformation snapshots.
Grammar --> Grammar : Original / transformed rules and steps\nor GrammarError
deactivate Grammar
opt Valid bounded transformation
  Grammar -> Grammar : calculate_first(); calculate_follow();\nbuild_table(); remaining-cycle checks
  activate Grammar
  Grammar --> Grammar : Sets, unambiguous cells, conflicts, warnings
  deactivate Grammar
end
Grammar --> API : Grammar analysis / GrammarError
deactivate Grammar
alt Valid grammar result (possibly not LL(1))
  API -> Lexer : lexical_report(saved corpus) or tokens_for(text)
  activate Lexer
  note over Lexer : Approved non-conflicting Word annotations;\nregex + lists + heuristics; preserve UNKNOWN.\nCorpus limits apply to analyze, not the practice field.
  Lexer --> API : Token streams / lexical report or storage error
  deactivate Lexer
  loop Each corpus entry, or one practice input
    API -> Parser : parse_analysis(grammar, tokens)
    activate Parser
    alt Conflicts or unresolved recursion
      note over Parser : Reject without choosing a conflicting production.
    else LL(1) table available
      note over Parser : Bounded stack machine; snapshots before actions.\nAccept only full input + end marker agreement.\nMissing cells/mismatch/trailing input/limits reject.
    end
    Parser --> API : accepted, error, trace, consumed
    deactivate Parser
  end
else Invalid notation / unsafe expansion / limits
  note over API : GrammarError maps to HTTP 422.
end
API --> Web : Structured results / safe error
deactivate API
Web --> Learner : Tables and traces; editor not implicitly saved
deactivate Web
legend bottom
  Function-module self-calls deliberately collapse internal function boundaries.
  No Gemini call determines analysis or acceptance.
  Existing CSV/audio are read-only; missing storage can bootstrap an empty header.
endlegend
@enduml
